# {{.ServiceName}} Proto

{{.Description}} Protocol Buffer definitions.

## Dependencies

### 1. Install protoc compiler

```bash
# macOS
brew install protobuf

# Ubuntu/Debian
apt-get install -y protobuf-compiler

# Verify installation
protoc --version
```

### 2. Install Go plugins

```bash
# Install protoc-gen-go (generates Go structs)
go install google.golang.org/protobuf/cmd/protoc-gen-go@latest

# Install protoc-gen-go-grpc (generates gRPC service code)
go install google.golang.org/grpc/cmd/protoc-gen-go-grpc@latest

# Ensure $GOPATH/bin is in PATH
export PATH="$PATH:$(go env GOPATH)/bin"
```

## Generate Code

```bash
# In proto/{{.ServiceNameLower}} directory
make gen

# Or manually
protoc --go_out=. --go_opt=paths=source_relative \
       --go-grpc_out=. --go-grpc_opt=paths=source_relative \
       {{.ServiceNameLower}}.proto
```

## Generated Files

- `{{.ServiceNameLower}}.pb.go` - Message struct definitions
- `{{.ServiceNameLower}}_grpc.pb.go` - gRPC service interface and client

## Usage Example

```go
import (
    pb "{{.ProjectModule}}/proto/{{.ServiceNameLower}}"
)

// Server implementation
type server struct {
    pb.Unimplemented{{.ServiceName}}ServiceServer
}

func (s *server) Hello(ctx context.Context, req *pb.HelloRequest) (*pb.HelloResponse, error) {
    return &pb.HelloResponse{
        Message: "Hello, " + req.Name,
    }, nil
}
```

## Test with grpcurl

```bash
# List services
grpcurl -plaintext localhost:{{.GRPCPort}} list

# Call Hello
grpcurl -plaintext -d '{"name":"World"}' localhost:{{.GRPCPort}} {{.ServiceNameLower}}.{{.ServiceName}}Service/Hello
```
